<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Real-World LM Validation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">RKSP and KSS generalize beyond synthetic tasks to real-world LMs. Table <a href="#S5.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ 5.4 Real-World LM Validation ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ Residual Koopman Spectral Profiling for Predicting and Preventing Transformer Training Instability" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> demonstrates this generalization with WikiText-103 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Merity et al., 2017</a>]</cite> and OpenWebText experiments. Benefits with KSS persist on real data, manifesting in three ways. First, divergence decreases by 2<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> to 5<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> across model sizes. Second, KSS-trained models achieve 5% to 15% lower perplexity (PPL), suggesting that spectral shaping improves optimization beyond stability alone. Third, KSS enables 1.5<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> to 2<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> higher learning rates, accelerating convergence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>KSS improves stability and PPL. Pre-LN normalization with 24 trials per configuration. Measured on WikiText-103 and OpenWebText language-modeling tasks.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T8.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:67.3pt;vertical-align:-31.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-47.9pt,9.3pt) scale(0.782638747352657,0.782638747352657) ;">
<table id="S5.T8.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<th id="S5.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><span id="S5.T8.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Model</span></th>
