<section id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">KAN</h5>

<div id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A9.T18" title="Table 18 ‣ KAN ‣ Appendix I Novel Architecture Case Studies ‣ Residual Koopman Spectral Profiling for Predicting and Preventing Transformer Training Instability" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a> reports KAN spectral diagnostics and KSS outcomes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024</a>]</cite>. KAN shows high normalized linear-fit error: B-spline basis functions produce <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}\approx[0.78,0.82]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>nl</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.78</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.82</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}\approx[0.78,0.82]</annotation></semantics></math>, higher than the typical transformer layers with <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.4,0.7]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.7</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.4,0.7]</annotation></semantics></math>. Despite this high <math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>η</mi><mi>nl</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}</annotation></semantics></math>, RKSP remains informative—ResDMD filtering enables spectral analysis for 68% to 78% of modes. KSS benefits KAN with a 3<math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> to 4<math id="A9.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> divergence reduction, suggesting that spectral shaping is architecture-agnostic.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A9.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span>KAN transformer with RKSP analysis. The B-spline nonlinearity challenges linear approximation. The B-spline order is <math id="A9.T18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>. We use <math id="A9.T18.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=256</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A9.T18.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=6</annotation></semantics></math>, and 24 trials. Measured on the synthetic LM task with random-token next-token prediction.</figcaption>
<table id="A9.T18.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A9.T18.2.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">
<th id="A9.T18.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><span id="A9.T18.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Model</span></th>
<th id="A9.T18.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><math id="A9.T18.m7" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">η</mi><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">nl</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta_{\mathrm{nl}}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A9.T18.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><math id="A9.T18.m8" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="M_{\approx 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">M</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">≈</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{\approx 1}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A9.T18.2.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><math id="A9.T18.m9" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;" mathbackground="#E6E6E6">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="A9.T18.2.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.6pt 4.5pt;"><span id="A9.T18.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6E6E6;">Div. of 24</span></th>
